Build 029, from the 028 console runs and the independent 028 review:
- Frame capture readers.txt: a capture request now arms one frame in which every texture or storage
  image a draw or dispatch binds is recorded (image address, view layers, the binding programs), and
  the capture follows at that frame's end. writers.txt only named the last writer of an image; in 028
  the "composite" e82daf057f4b81d6 turned out to sample no texture at all, so the pass that blends
  the fog layer was unknown. readers.txt gives the producer -> consumer edges of the captured frame.
- EDEN_DEDICATED_IMAGES (with the 5 s VMA lines): live dedicated image allocations, their bytes, how
  many were made and freed and the smallest. The 028c run with a 1 MiB threshold ended in a PS5
  CE-108255-1 with 1.6 GiB free; these counts show what the threshold actually does.

